{{#*inline "page"}}
<div class="hero">
    <h1 class="hero-title"><span class="gradient-text">Make your URLs this <span
                class="non-transparent">🤏</span> short</span></h1><br>
    <span class="subtitle">pinch.to produces the shortest links in the world by using the full spectrum of unicode characters.</span>
    <div id="box">
        <form action="/" method="post">
            <!-- <label for="url_long">Enter your long URL here:</label> -->
            <input placeholder="Paste your long URL here" pattern="\s*\S+[.:]\S+\s*" title="A web address, like example.com/page" required autofocus id="url_long"
                name="url_long">
            <button id="submit" type="submit">Shorten Now!</button>
        </form>
        {{#if error}}<p class="error">{{error}}</p>{{/if}}
    </div>


</div>

<div class="results-scroll">
    <div class="results">
        <b class="results-head">Recently shortened URLs</b>
                <table class="results-table {{new}}">
                    <tr class="header">
                        <th class="short_url">Short Link</th>
                        <th class="long_url">Original Link</th>
                        <th class="qr">QR</th>
                        <th class="clicks">Clicks</th>
                        <th class="date">Date</th>
                    </tr>
                    {{#each links}}
                    <tr class="body">
                        <td class="short_url"><input class="short_url" type="text" aria-label="Shortened URL"
                                value="{{../server_url}}/{{short_url}}" readonly>
                            <img class="copy" src="/static/copy.svg"
                                alt="{{../server_url}}/{{short_url}}">
                        </td>
                        <td class="long_url">
                            <span class="no_linebreak">
                                {{#if favicon_host}}<img class="favicon" src="/favicon/{{favicon_host}}" alt="" />{{/if}}
                                <a href="{{../server_url}}/{{short_url}}" rel="ugc nofollow">{{display_url}}</a>
                            </span>
                        </td>
                        <td class="qr"><img class="qr" src="/qr/{{short_url}}" alt="">
                        </td>
                        <td class="clicks">{{clicks}}</td>
                        <td class="date"><span class="timestamp">{{timestamp}}</span></td>
                    </tr>
                    {{/each}}

                </table>
    </div>
</div>
{{!-- <p class="bottom">
    So far, <b>{{url_counter}}</b> short URLs have been created.
</p> --}}
<div class="blog home-info">
    <h2>The shortest URL shortener in the world</h2>
    <p>A pinch.to link has seven characters. Other shorteners need nine to twenty for a new link:</p>
    <div class="blog-scroll">
        <table class="compare">
            <tr class="us"><td>pinch.to</td><td><code>🤏.to/ꙮ𐐀</code></td><td class="num">7</td></tr>
            <tr><td>T.LY</td><td><code>t.ly/abcd</code></td><td class="num">9</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Bitly</td><td><code>bit.ly/3xYz9Ab</code></td><td class="num">14</td></tr>
            <tr><td>TinyURL</td><td><code>tinyurl.com/2y5nzyk7</code></td><td class="num">20</td></tr>
        </table>
    </div>
    <p><a href="/blog/shortest-url-shorteners">The full comparison, with how we measured</a></p>

    <h3>What is the shortest URL possible?</h3>
    <p>A domain has at least four characters: one letter, a dot and a two-letter ending, like <code>t.co</code> or
        <code>🤏.to</code>. After the slash, other shorteners use four to ten Latin letters and digits. pinch.to uses two
        letters from all of Unicode's scripts, which is enough for 17 billion links.</p>

    <h3>Do the links work everywhere?</h3>
    <p>Browsers open them. Some apps do not turn an emoji domain into a clickable link; there, send
        <code>pinch.to/ꙮ𐐀</code> instead. Every code works on both domains.</p>

    <h3>Are they shorter in bytes, too?</h3>
    <p>No. Browsers send <code>🤏.to/ꙮ𐐀</code> as <code>xn--rp9h.to/%EA%99%AE%F0%90%90%80</code>, and the
        characters are hard to type. pinch.to links are short to look at, on a screen or on paper.</p>

    <h3>Is it free?</h3>
    <p>Yes, with no account, no ads and no trackers. The <a href="https://github.com/vongaisberg/unishort">source code
            is on GitHub</a>. Every link appears in the public list above, so do not shorten anything private.
        <a href="/blog/about">More about how pinch.to works</a>.</p>
</div>
<script type="application/ld+json">
{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "WebApplication", "name": "pinch.to",
 "url": "https://pinch.to/", "applicationCategory": "UtilitiesApplication", "operatingSystem": "Any",
 "description": "The shortest URL shortener in the world: links of two Unicode characters, like 🤏.to/ꙮ𐐀.",
 "offers": {"@type": "Offer", "price": "0", "priceCurrency": "USD"}}
</script>
{{/inline}}
{{> layout title="pinch.to - Shortest URL Shortener in the World"
path="/"
description="Shorten any link to two characters, like 🤏.to/ꙮ𐐀. pinch.to uses the whole Unicode range to make the shortest URLs in the world. Free, no sign-up, no trackers."}}